build/
*.keystore
hs_err_pid*.log
alpha.apk
# android/build.sh writes its APK next to itself, so the rule has to be anchored
# there. A bare "Phone-Dialer.apk" matched the filename in every directory,
# including apk/, where the published, installable build is kept and tracked.
# Git only consults this file for untracked paths, so the tracked
# apk/Phone-Dialer.apk survived — but the next time a run replaced it, a plain
# `git add apk/Phone-Dialer.apk` would have been refused without -f, and the
# repository would have gone on shipping the previous build's APK under a new
# version number with nothing to show that it had gone wrong.
/android/Phone-Dialer.apk
